  "rationale": "The previous implementation replaced suffixes with literal zeros, which broke values like \"2.1k\" (producing 2.1 instead of 2100) and omitted word\u2011based numbers. The new parser explicitly handles currency strings, plain numbers, decimal\u2011or\u2011integer \"k\" suffixes, and the three observed English phrases, converting all other tokens to NaN. This preserves the numeric meaning of the 12 recognized source values and only creates NaN for truly unparseable entries.",
